---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Metaphysical Secrets | Pranjal" description="A private metaphysical notebook." bodyClass="secrets-page">
  <Nav />
  <main class="secrets-shell">
    <a class="secrets-back" href={base + "about/pranjal/"}>← Photos &amp; words</a>

    <section class="secrets-gate" data-secrets-gate>
      <p class="gate-number">02 · Private notebook</p>
      <h1>Metaphysical<br /><em>secrets</em></h1>
      <p class="riddle-notice" data-riddle-notice>The riddle will be revealed after three failed attempts.</p>
      <blockquote data-gate-riddle hidden>
        I wear no robes of gold or silk, no crown upon my head,<br />
        I track the wild boar through the snows where mortal men feel dread.<br />
        I am the rugged mountain man, a simple hunter born,<br />
        Who challenged the greatest archer’s pride and left his spirit torn.<br />
        Yet look beneath my rustic mask, beyond the bow I wield<br />
        For I am the Lord of the Cosmic Dance, on the peak revealed.
      </blockquote>
      <form data-secrets-form autocomplete="off">
        <label for="secrets-answer" data-answer-label>Enter the password</label>
        <div><input id="secrets-answer" name="answer" type="password" spellcheck="false" required /><button type="submit">Enter</button></div>
        <p class="gate-error" data-gate-error aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
      <noscript>JavaScript is required to answer the riddle.</noscript>
    </section>

    <article class="secrets-content" data-secrets-content hidden>
      <header class="secrets-header">
        <p>02 · Private notebook</p>
        <h1>Metaphysical<br /><em>secrets</em></h1>
        <p class="secrets-deck">Five passages from the Vana Parva in which the Himalaya appears as both physical country and the threshold of another order.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="secrets-rule" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

      <section class="textual-note">
        <p class="passage-number">I</p>
        <div class="passage-body">
          <p class="passage-source">Vana Parva 3.141.25</p>
          <h2>Himavat, frequented by celestial beings</h2>
          <blockquote class="sanskrit" lang="sa">
            किराततङ्गणाकीर्णं कुणिन्दशतसंकुलम् ।<br />
            हिमवत्यमरैर्जुष्टं बह्वाश्चर्यसमाकुलम् ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="translation">
            <p class="translation-label">Translation</p>
            <p>“The Himalayan region was filled with Kirātas and Taṅgaṇas and populated by hundreds of Kuṇindas; it was frequented by celestial beings and filled with many wonders.”</p>
          </div>
          <p>The verse places the ordinary peoples of the Himalaya and the <i>amaras</i>, the deathless or celestial beings, within one layered geography. It does not carry the reader away from the mountain. The strange and the inhabited occupy the same terrain.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="textual-note">
        <p class="passage-number">II</p>
        <div class="passage-body">
          <p class="passage-source">Vana Parva 3.142.23</p>
          <h2>Gandhamādana, inhabited by Yakṣas</h2>
          <blockquote class="sanskrit" lang="sa">
            विशाला बदरी यत्र नरनारायणाश्रमः ।<br />
            तं सदाध्युषितं यक्षैर्द्रक्ष्यामो गिरिमुत्तमम् ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="translation">
            <p class="translation-label">Translation</p>
            <p>“There lies the vast Badarī, where stands the hermitage of Nara and Nārāyaṇa. We shall behold that supreme mountain, perpetually inhabited by Yakṣas.”</p>
          </div>
          <p>Badarī, the Nara and Nārāyaṇa hermitage, Gandhamādana, and the presence of Yakṣas are joined in a single sacred topography. Yakṣas are not extraterrestrials in a modern sense. They belong to a non-human class associated with wilderness, mountains, concealed wealth, and Kubera.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="textual-note">
        <p class="passage-number">III</p>
        <div class="passage-body">
          <p class="passage-source">Vana Parva 3.156.19–20</p>
          <h2>Music beyond the accessible mountain</h2>
          <blockquote class="sanskrit" lang="sa">
            अस्य चोपरि शैलस्य श्रूयते पर्वसंधिषु ।<br />
            भेरीपणवशङ्खानां मृदङ्गानां च निस्वनः ॥<br /><br />
            इहस्थैरेव तत्सर्वं श्रोतव्यं भरतर्षभाः ।<br />
            न कार्या वः कथंचित्स्यात्तत्राभिसरणे मतिः ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="translation">
            <p class="translation-label">Translation</p>
            <p>“Above this mountain, at the seasonal junctions, the sounds of kettledrums, smaller drums, conches, and mṛdaṅgas are heard.</p>
            <p>You must hear all this while remaining here, O bulls of the Bharatas. Under no circumstances should you form the intention of approaching that place.”</p>
          </div>
          <p>The Pāṇḍavas may hear what lies beyond the boundary, but they are expressly forbidden to cross it. Perception is permitted. Entry is not.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="textual-note textual-note--threshold">
        <p class="passage-number">IV</p>
        <div class="passage-body">
          <p class="passage-source">Vana Parva 3.156.21</p>
          <h2>“That route is not human”</h2>
          <blockquote class="sanskrit" lang="sa">
            न चाप्यतः परं शक्यं गन्तुं भरतसत्तमाः ।<br />
            विहारो ह्यत्र देवानाममानुषगतिस्तु सा ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="translation">
            <p class="translation-label">Translation</p>
            <p>“It is not possible for you to proceed beyond this point, O best of the Bharatas. This is the recreation-ground of the gods; that route is an <i>amānuṣa-gati</i>, a course not accessible to humans.”</p>
          </div>
          <p>This is the passage closest to what a modern reader might call a portal. Yet the Sanskrit deserves more care than that word permits. <i>Gati</i> can mean path, course, access, destination, or mode of existence. <i>Amānuṣa</i> means non-human, superhuman, or outside ordinary humanity.</p>
          <p>A “non-human passage” is therefore defensible. An “interdimensional portal” remains a modern, speculative interpretation.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="textual-note">
        <p class="passage-number">V</p>
        <div class="passage-body">
          <p class="passage-source">Vana Parva 3.156.23</p>
          <h2>Beyond the summit, the Siddha-world appears</h2>
          <blockquote class="sanskrit" lang="sa">
            अभ्यतिक्रम्य शिखरं शैलस्यास्य युधिष्ठिर ।<br />
            गतिः परमसिद्धानां देवर्षीणां प्रकाशते ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="translation">
            <p class="translation-label">Translation</p>
            <p>“Beyond the summit of this mountain, O Yudhiṣṭhira, the path, or realm, of the supreme Siddhas and divine Ṛṣis becomes manifest.”</p>
          </div>
          <p>This may be the Mahābhārata’s strongest metaphysical image of the Himalaya. Its terms are exact: <i>abhyatikramya śikharam</i>, having passed beyond the summit; <i>gatiḥ</i>, path, state, destiny, or realm; <i>parama-siddhānām</i>, of the highest perfected beings; and <i>prakāśate</i>, becomes visible or manifests.</p>
          <p>The summit reads as a threshold. Beyond it, a normally concealed order does not merely exist. It becomes perceptible.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <footer class="secrets-colophon">
        <p>All references are to the Vana Parva of the Mahābhārata. Translation and interpretive notes are presented here for close reading.</p>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(body.secrets-page) { background:#eae8e1; color:#211c18; }
  [hidden] { display:none!important; }
  .secrets-shell { width:min(1050px,calc(100% - 2rem)); min-height:92svh; margin:auto; padding:8rem 0 6rem; font-family:"Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  .secrets-back,.gate-number,.secrets-content>p { font:500 .66rem/1.5 "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .secrets-back { color:#5d554c; text-decoration:none; }
  .secrets-gate,.secrets-content { width:min(49rem,100%); margin:clamp(4rem,9vh,7rem) auto 0; }
  h1 { margin:1rem 0 2.5rem; font:500 clamp(3.7rem,9vw,8rem)/.82 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; letter-spacing:-.055em; }
  h1 em { color:inherit; font-style:normal; font-weight:500; }
  .riddle-notice { margin:0; color:#665d53; font:500 .72rem/1.55 "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.06em; }
  blockquote { margin:2rem 0 0; border-left:1px solid #8f8172; padding-left:clamp(1rem,3vw,2.3rem); color:#3f3831; font-size:clamp(1rem,1.7vw,1.3rem); line-height:1.8; }
  form { margin-top:3rem; }
  label,.gate-error,.gate-hint { font:500 .7rem/1.55 "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.06em; }
  form>div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto; margin-top:.7rem; border-bottom:1px solid #81715e; }
  input { min-width:0; border:0; padding:.9rem 0; outline:0; background:transparent; color:#211c18; font:400 1.2rem "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  button { border:0; padding:.9rem 0 .9rem 1.5rem; background:transparent; color:#bd674c; font:600 .68rem "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; cursor:pointer; }
  .gate-error { min-height:1.2rem; margin-top:.8rem; color:#9f3d29; }
  .secrets-content { width:min(58rem,100%); text-align:left; }
  .secrets-header { max-width:49rem; margin-inline:auto; }
  .secrets-deck { max-width:39rem; margin:-.5rem 0 3rem; color:#51483f; font:400 clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.5rem)/1.5 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  .secrets-rule { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1rem; color:#bd674c; }
  .secrets-rule::before,.secrets-rule::after { content:""; height:1px; flex:1; background:#5d5043; }
  .textual-note { display:grid; grid-template-columns:4rem minmax(0,1fr); gap:clamp(1rem,4vw,3.5rem); padding:clamp(3.5rem,8vw,6.5rem) 0; border-bottom:1px solid rgb(93 80 67/.38); }
  .passage-number { margin:.3rem 0 0; color:#bd674c; font:italic 400 1.15rem/1 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  .passage-body { max-width:45rem; }
  .passage-source,.translation-label { margin:0 0 .75rem; color:#765f4f; font:600 .62rem/1.5 "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .passage-body h2 { max-width:40rem; margin:0 0 2rem; font:500 clamp(2rem,5vw,4.2rem)/.98 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; letter-spacing:-.035em; }
  .sanskrit { margin:0; border:0; padding:clamp(1.4rem,4vw,2.4rem); color:#281f19; background:rgb(255 255 255/.34); font:400 clamp(1.05rem,2.1vw,1.45rem)/1.9 "Noto Serif Devanagari","Noto Serif",serif; }
  .translation { margin:2rem 0; padding-left:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem); border-left:2px solid #bd674c; }
  .translation p:not(.translation-label) { margin:.55rem 0 0; font:italic 400 clamp(1.05rem,1.8vw,1.28rem)/1.65 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  .passage-body>p:not(.passage-source) { max-width:42rem; margin:1.1rem 0 0; color:#3f3831; font:400 clamp(1rem,1.55vw,1.14rem)/1.75 "Louize Trial",Georgia,serif; }
  .passage-body i { font-style:italic; }
  .textual-note--threshold { margin-inline:clamp(-1rem,-2vw,-2rem); padding-inline:clamp(1rem,2vw,2rem); background:rgb(189 103 76/.055); }
  .secrets-colophon { max-width:45rem; margin:3rem 0 0 auto; color:#665d53; font:500 .68rem/1.65 "Neue Montreal Trial",Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:.035em; }
  @media(max-width:620px) {
    .secrets-shell { padding-top:6.5rem; }
    .textual-note { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:.8rem; }
    .passage-number { font-size:.95rem; }
    .sanskrit { margin-inline:-.25rem; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const gate = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-secrets-gate]");
  const content = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-secrets-content]");
  const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>("[data-secrets-form]");
  const answer = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#secrets-answer");
  const error = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gate-error]");
  const riddle = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gate-riddle]");
  const riddleNotice = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-riddle-notice]");
  const answerLabel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-answer-label]");
  const SESSION_KEY = "metaphysical-secrets-unlocked";
  const ANSWER_HASH = "aff8acff11671fe1a4f9be4344b33462784655ffbc86ca95f78b78809e9ced3c";
  let failedAttempts = 0;

  const reveal = () => {
    if (gate) gate.hidden = true;
    if (content) content.hidden = false;
  };

  const digest = async (value: string) => {
    const bytes = await crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", new TextEncoder().encode(value));
    return Array.from(new Uint8Array(bytes), (byte) => byte.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
  };

  if (sessionStorage.getItem(SESSION_KEY) === "yes") reveal();

  form?.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const value = answer?.value.trim().toLowerCase() || "";
    if (await digest(value) === ANSWER_HASH) {
      sessionStorage.setItem(SESSION_KEY, "yes");
      if (error) error.textContent = "";
      reveal();
      return;
    }
    failedAttempts += 1;
    if (error) error.textContent = failedAttempts < 3 ? "The mountain remains closed." : "The riddle has been revealed.";
    if (failedAttempts >= 3) {
      if (riddle) riddle.hidden = false;
      if (riddleNotice) riddleNotice.hidden = true;
      if (answerLabel) answerLabel.textContent = "Who am I?";
    }
    if (answer) { answer.value = ""; answer.focus(); }
  });
</script>
